      "description": "The reconstruction (reconstructed.png) was drawn from the elements parsed from the OCR HTML output (ocr_html.html): each element of the types the variant evaluates is drawn at its detected bounding box on a blank white canvas at the original page resolution. Text is drawn with fonts fitted to each box using measurements of the original page; formulas are rasterised with matplotlib mathtext, with pdflatex used for block LaTeX environments and as a fallback; tables are drawn by parsing the element's HTML and drawing the cell grid. In ocr_all_no_mask, the original pixels of detected image regions are copied into the reconstruction. Fonts, glyph shapes and line breaks may differ from the original page scans.",
