      "description": "Training triplets for the docsim_triplets config were constructed by: (1) computing Hungarian-matched edit distance between OCR-extracted text and OmniDocBench ground-truth text for each page to obtain a numeric fidelity score; (2) pairing each anchor (the masked_original.png of a page in the ocr_all, ocr_all_no_mask or ocr_text variant) with a positive (a low-error reconstructed.png of the same page and variant) and a negative (a high-error reconstructed.png of an unrelated page), requiring an edit-distance gap of at least 0.15 between positive and negative. The edit distance uses element-level Levenshtein distance with linear-sum-assignment matching, normalised by maximum string length. All 20,280 triplets are cross-page; they draw on 710 of the 1,355 pages (371 as anchors). Fully automated; no human annotation was performed.",
